<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lodi dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lodi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lodi dynasty was an Afghan dynasty that ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> from 1451 to 1526, the last of its ruling houses. Its final sultan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-lodi">Ibrahim Lodi</a>, was defeated and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>, a Timurid prince, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-panipat">First Battle of Panipat</a> in 1526. This victory ended the Delhi Sultanate and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty.jpg" alt="Lodi dynasty" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maps created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan Territorial area: पाटलिपुत्र (talk), per Schwar... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Lodis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
